WEBVTT

00:00:06.632 --> 00:00:11.929
STUDIO RIKKA

00:00:46.421 --> 00:00:48.215
The archives that we call "history”

00:00:48.465 --> 00:00:50.425
ceased to exist at some point.

00:00:51.593 --> 00:00:53.178
Before we knew it

00:00:54.221 --> 00:00:55.847
humans were living in this world.

00:01:11.113 --> 00:01:12.614
Restoration in progress

00:01:12.614 --> 00:01:13.740
Restoration complete

00:01:33.260 --> 00:01:34.094
Good.

00:01:37.723 --> 00:01:38.974
Power saving mode

00:01:42.352 --> 00:01:43.395
Audio connection

00:01:43.395 --> 00:01:44.438
Oh? Are you done?

00:01:44.438 --> 00:01:46.106
Yeah. It's a visual record, after all.

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:48.609
Got it. I'll get the next one ready.

00:01:48.859 --> 00:01:50.611
The atmosphere is clear,

00:01:50.611 --> 00:01:51.987
with lots of greenery.

00:01:52.821 --> 00:01:55.532
It's a record of the surface layer
from around AD 2000.

00:01:56.283 --> 00:01:58.785
- The location...
-Who cares about the location?

00:01:59.411 --> 00:02:02.664
Ura, I'm always telling you...

00:02:02.664 --> 00:02:05.834
"Don't bother with the
Analysis Department's work."

00:02:06.209 --> 00:02:07.544
Understood.

00:02:07.711 --> 00:02:09.171
Send the next one.

00:02:12.883 --> 00:02:15.052
Analysis Division - 055 Transfer
Restored/Not analyzed

00:02:32.903 --> 00:02:34.613
Population explosion

00:02:41.703 --> 00:02:43.538
I'm sending two together.

00:02:44.164 --> 00:02:45.248
It has lots of encryption.

00:02:45.415 --> 00:02:47.584
I'll try opening them.

00:02:51.129 --> 00:02:51.630
Opening

00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:52.089
Opened

00:02:56.385 --> 00:02:57.094
What?!

00:02:57.761 --> 00:02:58.387
What happened?

00:02:58.804 --> 00:02:59.721
This is unusual.

00:03:00.055 --> 00:03:01.682
It's a visual record with sound.

00:03:02.182 --> 00:03:03.767
This is worth restoring.

00:03:04.726 --> 00:03:06.812
- Oh.
- Until tomorrow.

00:03:07.270 --> 00:03:09.106
I'm disconnecting the book.

00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:11.316
Until tomorrow.

00:03:15.904 --> 00:03:18.615
Archival debris, lying dormant
throughout the world.

00:03:19.491 --> 00:03:23.954
Rare fragments from the former world.

00:03:24.538 --> 00:03:27.124
Restoration Division 080
Binary code that can be restored.

00:03:32.254 --> 00:03:35.507
That's why I was excavating archives.

00:03:36.633 --> 00:03:40.512
092 Archive Excavation Department Because these
are the only clues to understand the past.

00:03:51.982 --> 00:03:53.275
Clock out

00:03:54.067 --> 00:03:56.153
Clock out

00:04:20.927 --> 00:04:23.138
Come back when it's time to clock out.

00:04:23.138 --> 00:04:25.474
I'll go back if there's work
to do at the Analysis Division.

00:04:25.474 --> 00:04:26.349
Hey, Riko.

00:04:26.767 --> 00:04:28.393
Why do you always go up there?

00:04:28.685 --> 00:04:30.437
Looks like everyone's gone.

00:04:31.188 --> 00:04:33.940
< Elevator

00:04:40.322 --> 00:04:41.782
Why are you obsessed
with the Excavation Department?

00:04:41.948 --> 00:04:42.991
Because of the archives.

00:04:42.991 --> 00:04:46.161
Otherwise, I'd never come up to this level.

00:04:46.328 --> 00:04:48.246
Current level: Floor 0285 The Excavation
Department is the only thing left up here.

00:04:48.246 --> 00:04:50.081
Current level: Floor 0285 Closed The Excavation
Department is the only thing left up here.

00:04:50.457 --> 00:04:52.209
It'll move to a lower level eventually.

00:04:53.710 --> 00:04:58.173
They say the 80s-level Excavation
Departments will be closed off.

00:05:08.391 --> 00:05:10.477
There's work for you tomorrow.

00:05:10.477 --> 00:05:11.645
You found something again?

00:05:11.895 --> 00:05:13.480
I sent you one today.

00:05:13.730 --> 00:05:17.734
It's a surface-layer record,
before the sunlight was blocked.

00:05:18.652 --> 00:05:19.736
Green...

00:05:26.701 --> 00:05:32.499
Humans learned about this reality, along with
the past world, through excavated archives.

00:05:33.458 --> 00:05:34.960
The world in the beginning

00:05:35.460 --> 00:05:39.214
was covered by the artificial world

00:05:39.923 --> 00:05:41.716
and human beings lived in the gaps.

00:05:42.175 --> 00:05:43.718
The environmental maintenance equipment.

00:05:44.219 --> 00:05:47.722
And the lower levels, where
the equipment has the most impact.

00:05:56.189 --> 00:06:01.194
Below the lowest level, there's
an area called the ocean.

00:06:01.444 --> 00:06:05.699
According to the excavated archives,
humans came from the ocean.

00:06:06.199 --> 00:06:07.701
Meaning what...

00:06:07.951 --> 00:06:11.997
Lots of humans eke out
livings in the bottom layer.

00:06:52.037 --> 00:06:53.413
For the Analysis Division - 055 - Transfer

00:07:03.214 --> 00:07:05.342
Take a look at the record I just sent you.

00:07:05.926 --> 00:07:07.218
What is it this time?

00:07:07.928 --> 00:07:09.471
The green world again?

00:07:11.723 --> 00:07:13.475
Or human history?

00:07:13.683 --> 00:07:15.685
That's what I want to know.

00:07:16.436 --> 00:07:19.147
What's this a record of?

00:07:31.117 --> 00:07:32.243
What's that?

00:07:32.911 --> 00:07:33.745
Well...

00:07:35.455 --> 00:07:37.332
You should have brought me
the fully restored version.

00:07:52.639 --> 00:07:54.766
I got this far with simple restoration.

00:07:55.308 --> 00:07:56.726
The thing I'm curious about is...

00:07:57.310 --> 00:07:57.936
...this.

00:07:58.853 --> 00:08:02.232
Could it be...a book?

00:08:03.400 --> 00:08:04.985
It's probably a book.

00:08:04.985 --> 00:08:07.028
But doesn't it look strange?

00:08:07.195 --> 00:08:12.409
Originally books were a recording format
to transfer text and figures using a physical method.

00:08:12.742 --> 00:08:13.994
Like this.

00:08:14.452 --> 00:08:16.830
Of course, you could only do the recording once,

00:08:16.830 --> 00:08:18.999
and you couldn't communicate with other books.

00:08:19.374 --> 00:08:22.502
But it was a medium for passing on
archives, just like now.

00:08:22.919 --> 00:08:24.045
So this...

00:08:25.213 --> 00:08:26.756
...archive storage?

00:08:28.008 --> 00:08:31.511
Viewing records and putting them in a database.

00:08:31.928 --> 00:08:32.929
And then...

00:08:32.929 --> 00:08:34.723
Why are you obsessed
with the Excavation Department?

00:08:35.473 --> 00:08:36.933
You're not interested in knowing?

00:08:43.690 --> 00:08:45.442
Where are you going?

00:08:46.943 --> 00:08:48.820
Haven't you had enough?

00:08:52.949 --> 00:08:57.495
A lot more people used to work here.

00:08:59.914 --> 00:09:07.964
I heard it was crowded, and everyone
rejoiced when a new record was found.

00:09:10.467 --> 00:09:13.470
092 Archive Excavation
Department

00:09:14.596 --> 00:09:17.724
That's how I feel.

00:09:26.191 --> 00:09:28.443
Restoration in progress

00:09:33.031 --> 00:09:33.323
Restoration in progress

00:09:37.994 --> 00:09:38.912
Loading record

00:10:00.642 --> 00:10:02.602
Ocean

00:10:02.936 --> 00:10:04.938
Sky

00:10:04.938 --> 00:10:06.606
Pale Cocoon

00:10:19.619 --> 00:10:24.624
092 Archive
Excavation Department

00:10:47.438 --> 00:10:50.567
You forget 882: You — forget 883: You — do not
forget 884: 1 — forget you 884:1 — do not forget you

00:11:08.710 --> 00:11:10.211
How's the restoration going?

00:11:10.628 --> 00:11:11.754
It's odd.

00:11:12.714 --> 00:11:15.216
It's a jumble of image fragments.

00:11:15.216 --> 00:11:17.552
Same for the things the girl is saying.

00:11:17.552 --> 00:11:19.429
Restoration in progress
The restoration is almost done,

00:11:19.429 --> 00:11:21.389
but analysis might be tough.

00:11:22.599 --> 00:11:24.559
But that's not my job.

00:11:24.559 --> 00:11:27.312
No one showed up for work
in the Analysis Division again today.

00:11:27.312 --> 00:11:29.105
Riko's a no-show again, huh?

00:11:30.148 --> 00:11:33.860
It seems she wants to quit
the Excavation Department.

00:11:34.194 --> 00:11:36.946
Dunno... I haven't seen her recently.

00:11:39.115 --> 00:11:41.201
A long time ago, she said

00:11:42.035 --> 00:11:47.165
people leave records because there
are things they want to preserve.

00:11:47.332 --> 00:11:51.836
Of all the records we've excavated, is
there anything that still exists today?

00:11:53.880 --> 00:11:57.884
I'm...quitting...this job.

00:12:00.720 --> 00:12:01.638
Ura...

00:12:02.055 --> 00:12:05.308
Have you ever thought
the records might all be lies?

00:12:05.308 --> 00:12:08.478
All of the records have been verified.

00:12:08.478 --> 00:12:14.150
Ura... I often wish they were lies.

00:12:26.204 --> 00:12:29.165
"Environment" "Degradation”

00:13:42.905 --> 00:13:45.408
My grandma that said when she was a child,

00:13:46.075 --> 00:13:48.995
people lived in the levels up there.

00:13:52.373 --> 00:13:56.753
The environment maintenance equipment
used to reach the higher levels.

00:13:57.670 --> 00:13:59.297
I heard eventually they couldn't live up there,

00:13:59.297 --> 00:14:01.507
so they came down here.

00:14:02.050 --> 00:14:05.261
Did you know some people
kept on living up there?

00:14:05.470 --> 00:14:07.347
My grandma was one of them.

00:14:08.306 --> 00:14:12.643
The world in the archives that didn't
need environment maintenance equipment...

00:14:13.227 --> 00:14:17.398
They didn't want to accept a reality
so completely different from that world.

00:14:17.398 --> 00:14:19.275
What's up there?

00:14:19.984 --> 00:14:21.361
Then...

00:14:23.112 --> 00:14:25.073
She fell down from above.

00:14:28.826 --> 00:14:30.370
This is where her body landed.

00:14:31.287 --> 00:14:34.123
They said her insides were in bad shape.

00:14:35.792 --> 00:14:39.128
Even though you can't live beyond the reach
of the environment maintenance equipment.

00:14:39.128 --> 00:14:41.297
Maybe if we researched the archives more...?

00:14:46.386 --> 00:14:49.389
Will digging up archives change this world?

00:14:49.389 --> 00:14:51.808
- We can understand.
- I wish I didn't understand.

00:14:52.183 --> 00:14:57.897
The green world, and that
humans destroyed that world.

00:14:58.481 --> 00:15:01.150
I don't want to lose any more hope in reality.

00:15:02.819 --> 00:15:07.323
We shouldn't have dug up
the archives in the first place.

00:15:07.698 --> 00:15:12.328
No one wants to see more
of humanity's foolishness.

00:15:12.745 --> 00:15:15.415
Don't you get it?

00:15:15.957 --> 00:15:16.833
I got it.

00:15:18.835 --> 00:15:20.503
I understood.

00:15:21.003 --> 00:15:21.629
Right.

00:15:23.548 --> 00:15:26.217
It's something everyone understands.

00:15:28.845 --> 00:15:35.351
Major environmental change inevitable
as population growth impacts resources.

00:15:40.523 --> 00:15:41.816
So what about me?

00:15:42.900 --> 00:15:45.695
Did I just want to surround
myself with the archives?

00:15:47.113 --> 00:15:52.368
To avoid seeing this reality,
the ruin of a huge relocation camp.

00:15:53.995 --> 00:15:56.372
Restoration in progress
But, back then...

00:15:56.873 --> 00:16:02.879
I longed to find something from
the world of the archives in this reality.

00:16:03.671 --> 00:16:05.381
That's what I was thinking.

00:16:31.282 --> 00:16:32.658
What was she looking at?

00:16:37.622 --> 00:16:39.916
Restoration in progress

00:16:40.124 --> 00:16:41.167
Restoration complete

00:16:43.169 --> 00:16:49.967
Morning when the woods have fallen asleep

00:16:50.593 --> 00:16:56.557
Smoke leaves a trail in the sky

00:16:57.141 --> 00:17:03.689
Intersecting with the horizon

00:17:04.273 --> 00:17:10.863
Creating a silver cross

00:17:11.280 --> 00:17:18.120
Morning when the ocean has fallen asleep

00:17:18.871 --> 00:17:25.086
The moon has stopped waiting

00:17:25.586 --> 00:17:32.009
The full moon wanes, offering a cradle

00:17:32.552 --> 00:17:39.642
In place of a prayer

00:17:40.893 --> 00:17:46.566
The last angel

00:17:48.067 --> 00:17:53.656
The lingering horn

00:17:55.074 --> 00:18:00.788
Pale cocoon that can't hatch

00:18:02.164 --> 00:18:08.421
Even without a smile

00:18:09.630 --> 00:18:16.387
Morning when the stars have fallen asleep

00:18:17.179 --> 00:18:23.227
At least there is morning with a cloudy sky

00:18:23.644 --> 00:18:30.401
When there was god

00:18:30.860 --> 00:18:37.617
Wet and glistening garden strawberries

00:18:37.867 --> 00:18:44.624
Promising a day to meet

00:18:45.791 --> 00:18:50.046
I won't forget you

00:19:06.771 --> 00:19:09.148
Restoration in progress

00:19:16.614 --> 00:19:17.448
This is...

00:19:18.449 --> 00:19:19.492
...sky."

00:19:47.019 --> 00:19:49.855
When I'm here, I often wonder

00:19:50.231 --> 00:19:52.441
why people used to leave records behind.

00:19:52.733 --> 00:19:54.860
So what are you doing right now?

00:19:55.778 --> 00:19:58.864
Some things you want
always to stay the same, right?

00:19:58.864 --> 00:20:00.408
I'm recording!

00:20:10.710 --> 00:20:13.212
Restoration in progress

00:20:13.379 --> 00:20:14.630
Restoration complete

00:20:16.215 --> 00:20:20.678
Hello to everyone on earth
watching this show. I'm Yoko.

00:20:21.011 --> 00:20:24.056
I arrived here a week ago.

00:20:24.682 --> 00:20:27.435
I'm at a residential area
in the Sea of Tranquility.

00:20:28.060 --> 00:20:32.064
It seems this colony did everything first,

00:20:32.064 --> 00:20:33.149
and it's close to the harbor.

00:20:33.941 --> 00:20:38.320
And gravity is just like earth in places
with environment maintenance equipment.

00:20:38.529 --> 00:20:41.365
It's a lot more comfortable
than I expected.

00:20:42.658 --> 00:20:45.828
But.. when I look up at the sky,

00:20:46.078 --> 00:20:50.207
There's the rust-colored earth.

00:20:52.501 --> 00:20:53.210
Wait!

00:20:55.546 --> 00:21:01.010
I know it's tough for everyone waiting
for a place on the immigration ship.

00:21:01.302 --> 00:21:05.181
Let's hope for the best...

00:21:06.140 --> 00:21:09.852
...and that someday our mother star
will awaken from her long sleep,

00:21:10.186 --> 00:21:12.188
and dawn will come again...

00:21:12.730 --> 00:21:15.232
and that people will be there.

00:21:15.941 --> 00:21:18.736
Yoko and the "Pale Cocoon.”

00:21:34.710 --> 00:21:37.755
The rusted earth...

00:22:15.835 --> 00:22:16.877
Pale blue...

00:22:24.176 --> 00:22:26.262
